RayCAD patch to OCCT 8.0.1 (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception; this file is under the same terms).

What: ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreSurfdata, at "determination of neighbor surface", reads SurfData anInd of
myListStripe.First() although anInd was computed for the stripe at the current vertex (aStripe, whose sequence
is aSeqSurfData and is used everywhere else in the function). Read it from aSeqSurfData.

Why: when the vertex belongs to another stripe than the first one, the code reads the wrong stripe. If the first
stripe is shorter than anInd, NCollection_Sequence::Value is out of range; release builds have no range check, so
Find returns the last node and Value then leaves the sequence's cached position (myCurrentIndex) past its end. The
next lookup in that sequence walks off the list and dereferences a null node: ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter in
ChFi3d_Builder::Compute (access violation on Windows, SIGSEGV on Linux). Seen in RayCAD's naming random test (holdout
sequence 18:3, a 0.707 mm chamfer of two edges, BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer). When the first stripe is long enough,
the old code silently took the neighbour face from an unrelated SurfData. When the vertex's stripe is the first
one (every single-stripe blend) the two expressions are the same object, so nothing changes there.

Upstream: not fixed in OCCT master as of 2026-11-18 (the same two lines are still there). Not reported upstream yet.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
@@ -3898,14 +3898,16 @@ void ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreSurfdata(const int Index)
   }
 
   // determination of neighbor surface
+  // anInd indexes the SurfData of the stripe at this vertex (aSeqSurfData), which need not be the
+  // first stripe of the builder.
   int indSurface;
   if (is1stCP1OnArc)
   {
-    indSurface = myListStripe.First()->SetOfSurfData()->Value(anInd)->IndexOfS1();
+    indSurface = aSeqSurfData.Value(anInd)->IndexOfS1();
   }
   else
   {
-    indSurface = myListStripe.First()->SetOfSurfData()->Value(anInd)->IndexOfS2();
+    indSurface = aSeqSurfData.Value(anInd)->IndexOfS2();
   }
 
   aNeighborFace = TopoDS::Face(myDS->Shape(indSurface));
